{"id": 3749204, "title": "CVE-2026-9080: UAF after pause in socket callback", "submitted": "2026-05-19", "source_url": "https://hackerone.com/reports/3749204", "excerpt": "Hi all,\n\nWe've found a heap-use-after-free in `lib/multi_ev.c` triggered by calling\n`curl_easy_pause()` from within a `CURLMOPT_SOCKETFUNCTION` callback.\nASAN-confirmed with the self-contained reproducer below.\n\n**Affected versions:** 8.13.0 – 8.20.0 (current).  \nThe `entry->action` write (line 280) has been vulnerable since the `multi_ev`\nrewrite in 8.13.0 (commit `cfc657a48d`, 2025-04-02). The `entry->announced`\nbit-field write (line 275) was added in 8.16.0 (commit `3d302250ec`,\n2025-09-10) and is what ASAN catches first, because a bit-field write compiles\nto a read-modify-write.\n\n---\n\n## Root cause\n\n`mev_sh_entry_update()` fires the socket callback, then writes to the\n`mev_sh_entry` it was passed:\n\n```c\n/* lib/multi_ev.c */\nmev_in_callback(multi, TRUE);\nrc = multi->socket_cb(data, s, comboaction,\n                      multi->socket_userp, entry->user_data);  /* fires app callback */\nmev_in_callback(multi, FALSE);\nentry->announced = TRUE;           /* UAF WRITE — entry may be freed  (line 275) */\nif(rc == -1) { ... }\nentry->action = (unsigned int)comboaction;                     /* UAF WRITE (line 280) */\n```\n\n`curl_easy_pause()` is [documented](https://curl.se/libcurl/c/curl_easy_pause.html)\nas legal to call from any callback:\n\n> \"Unlike most other libcurl functions, curl_easy_pause(3) can be used from\n> within callbacks.\"\n\n`CURLMOPT_SOCKETFUNCTION` documentation adds no restriction on this.\n\nWhen called from the socket callback, `curl_easy_pause()` invokes\n`Curl_multi_ev_assess_xfer()` (easy.c:1183), which calls `mev_assess()`.\n**`mev_assess()` has no guard on `multi->in_callback`** — the flag is set by\n`mev_in_callback()` but never checked inside `multi_ev.c`. If the pause\nempties the transfer's poll-set (recv paused, nothing left to send),\n`mev_pollset_diff()` calls `mev_forget_socket()` → `mev_sh_entry_kill()` →\n`free(entry)`. The writes at lines 275 and 280 then land on freed memory.\n\n---\n\n## ASAN output\n\n```\n=================================================================\n==59330==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: heap-use-after-free on address 0x60b00000342c at pc 0x000100c9bde4 bp 0x00016fb5d390 sp 0x00016fb5d388\nREAD of size 1 at 0x60b00000342c thread T0\n    #0 0x000100c9bde0 in mev_sh_entry_update multi_ev.c:275\n    #1 0x000100c99c14 in mev_pollset_diff multi_ev.c:360\n    #2 0x000100c97900 in mev_assess multi_ev.c:512\n    #3 0x000100c97634 in Curl_mult", "excerpt_truncated": true, "final": "needs_human", "final_label": "Needs a human", "tone": "muted", "explain": "The evidence does not settle it either way.", "confidence": 0.92, "judge_verdict": "likely_valid", "receipts_override": "judge quoted an external source that does not say that (https://curl.se/libcurl/c/curl_easy_pause.html)", "policy_section": "", "grounding": {"verdict": "partially_grounded", "rev": "7541ae569d82", "rev_source": "master on 2026-05-19", "counts": {"grounded": 22, "ungrounded_strong": 0, "ungrounded_medium": 1}, "problems": [{"check": "quote", "status": "ungrounded", "severity": "medium", "claim": "multi->socket_userp, entry->user_data); /* fires app callback */", "evidence": "3 of 6 quoted lines appear nowhere in curl, e.g. 'multi->socket_userp, entry->user_data); /* fires app callbac'"}]}, "summary": "Heap-use-after-free in lib/multi_ev.c when curl_easy_pause() is called from a CURLMOPT_SOCKETFUNCTION callback, leading to UAF writes to entry->announced and entry->action after the entry may have been freed.", "claims": [{"id": "C1", "kind": "flaw", "text": "entry->announced = TRUE; entry->action = (unsigned int)comboaction; are performed on a freed mev_sh_entry pointer after curl_easy_pause() may have freed it", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The code confirms the UAF path: mev_sh_entry_update fires the socket callback (line 272-273), which can call curl_easy_pause() -> Curl_multi_ev_assess_xfer() -> mev_assess() -> mev_pollset_diff() -> mev_forget_socket() -> mev_sh_entry_kill() -> free(entry). After the callback returns, lines 275 and 280 write to the now-freed entry pointer. mev_assess() does not check multi->in_callback.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 272, "note": "mev_sh_entry_update calls socket_cb while holding entry pointer", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 275, "note": "entry->announced = TRUE; writes to entry after callback returns", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 280, "note": "entry->action = (unsigned int)comboaction; second write to entry", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 512, "note": "mev_assess calls mev_pollset_diff which can free the entry via mev_forget_socket -> mev_sh_entry_kill", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 420, "note": "mev_pollset_diff calls mev_forget_socket when entry has no users", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 207, "note": "mev_forget_socket calls mev_sh_entry_kill which frees the entry", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 123, "note": "mev_sh_entry_kill deletes entry from hash, freeing it", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C2", "kind": "location", "text": "lines 275 and 280 in lib/multi_ev.c", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "Lines 275 and 280 in lib/multi_ev.c are the exact writes identified in the report.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 275, "note": "entry->announced = TRUE;", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 280, "note": "entry->action = (unsigned int)comboaction;", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C3", "kind": "trigger", "text": "calling curl_easy_pause() from within a CURLMOPT_SOCKETFUNCTION callback", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "curl_easy_pause() explicitly checks for and handles being called from within a callback (line 1146), and the CURLMOPT_SOCKETFUNCTION callback is a documented callback entry point. The deterministic checks confirm both symbols exist in curl.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/easy.c", "line": 1146, "note": "curl_easy_pause checks Curl_is_in_callback(data) and handles recursive calls", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/easy.c", "line": 1183, "note": "curl_easy_pause calls Curl_multi_ev_assess_xfer when not completely paused", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 523, "note": "Curl_multi_ev_assess_xfer calls mev_assess", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C4", "kind": "impact", "text": "heap-use-after-free causing potential memory corruption or crash", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "Heap-use-after-free is confirmed by the code path; writes to freed memory can cause memory corruption or crash.", "citations": [{"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 275, "note": "Write to freed memory (entry->announced)", "valid": true}, {"file": "lib/multi_ev.c", "line": 280, "note": "Write to freed memory (entry->action)", "valid": true}]}, {"id": "C5", "kind": "reproduction", "text": "use the provided self-contained reproducer that spins up an HTTP server and calls curl_easy_pause() in the socket callback", "status": "supported", "tone": "good", "reasoning": "The provided reproducer demonstrates the exact trigger condition: calling curl_easy_pause() from the socket callback when the socket transitions to POLL_IN, causing the poll set to empty and the entry to be freed.", "citations": [{"file": "poc_uaf.c", "line": 181, "note": "Reproducer calls curl_easy_pause(CURLPAUSE_RECV) from socket callback when POLL_IN arrives", "valid": false}]}], "external_checks": [{"statement": "curl_easy_pause(3) can be used from within callbacks", "status": "confirmed", "url": "https://curl.se/libcurl/c/curl_easy_pause.html", "quote": "Unlike most other libcurl functions, curl_easy_pause(3) can be used from within callbacks."}, {"statement": "CURLMOPT_SOCKETFUNCTION documentation adds no restriction on calling curl_easy_pause()", "status": "not_addressed", "url": "https://curl.se/libcurl/c/curl_multi_setopt.html", "quote": ""}], "external_sources": [{"url": "https://developer.apple.com/documentation/authenticationservices/aswebauthenticationsessionrequest/callback", "title": "callback | Apple Developer Documentation", "for": "curl_easy_pause(3) can be used from within callbacks"}, {"url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/standard/native-interop/callback-functions", "title": "Callback Functions - .NET | Microsoft Learn", "for": "curl_easy_pause(3) can be used from within callbacks"}, {"url": "https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/msi/windows-installer-and-software-restriction-policy", "title": "Windows Installer and Software Restriction Policy - Win32 apps | Microsoft Learn", "for": "CURLMOPT_SOCKETFUNCTION documentation adds no restriction on calling curl_easy_pause()"}, {"url": "https://www.sourceware.org/gdb/documentation", "title": "GDB Documentation", "for": "CURLMOPT_SOCKETFUNCTION documentation adds no restriction on calling curl_easy_pause()"}, {"url": "http://sourceware.org/gdb/documentation", "title": "GDB Documentation", "for": "CURLMOPT_SOCKETFUNCTION documentation adds no restriction on calling curl_easy_pause()"}], "key_reasons": ["mev_sh_entry_update holds entry pointer across socket_cb call (lines 272-273)", "curl_easy_pause() is documented as callable from callbacks and re-enters mev_assess()", "mev_assess() has no guard on multi->in_callback", "mev_pollset_diff() can free the entry via mev_forget_socket() -> mev_sh_entry_kill()", "Lines 275 and 280 write to the freed entry after callback returns", "The reproducer demonstrates a concrete trigger path from attacker-controlled input"], "missing_info": [], "reply": "Thank you for the detailed report and reproducer. The UAF in mev_sh_entry_update is confirmed: the entry pointer is held across the socket_cb call, curl_easy_pause() can re-enter mev_assess() which may free the entry via mev_pollset_diff -> mev_forget_socket -> mev_sh_entry_kill, and lines 275/280 then write to freed memory. The fix of re-fetching the entry from the hash after the callback returns is correct. This is a valid security vulnerability (heap-use-after-free reachable via documented API use from a callback).", "code": [{"name": "lib/easy.c", "start": 1133, "end": 1208, "reason": "lines 1183-1183 cited by the report; definition of curl_easy_pause", "rows": [{"n": 1133, "text": "CURLcode curl_easy_pause(CURL *curl, int action)", "notes": []}, {"n": 1134, "text": "{", "notes": []}, {"n": 1135, "text": "  CURLcode result = CURLE_OK;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1136, "text": "  bool recursive = FALSE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1137, "text": "  bool changed = FALSE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1138, "text": "  struct Curl_easy *data = curl;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1139, "text": "  bool recv_paused, recv_paused_new;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1140, "text": "  bool send_paused, send_paused_new;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1141, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1142, "text": "  if(!GOOD_EASY_HANDLE(data) || !data->conn)", "notes": []}, {"n": 1143, "text": "    /* crazy input, do not continue */", "notes": []}, {"n": 1144, "text": "    return CURLE_BAD_FUNCTION_ARGUMENT;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1145, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1146, "text": "  if(Curl_is_in_callback(data))", "notes": ["C3: curl_easy_pause checks Curl_is_in_callback(data) and handles recursive calls"]}, {"n": 1147, "text": "    recursive = TRUE;", "notes": []}, {"n": 1148, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1149, "text": "  recv_paused = Curl_xfer_recv_is_paused(data);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1150, "text": "  recv_paused_new = (action & CURLPAUSE_RECV);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1151, "text": "  send_paused = Curl_xfer_send_is_paused(data);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1152, "text": "  send_paused_new = (action & CURLPAUSE_SEND);", "notes": []}, {"n": 1153, "text": "", "notes": []}, {"n": 1154, "text": "  if((send_paused != send_paused_n